WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.467
Once we understand the basic structure, we can begin a quick exploratory analysis.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:09.097
The describe method summarizes numerical columns.

00:00:09.097 --> 00:00:14.022
It can show the count, mean, standard deviation, minimum, quartiles, and maximum.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:19.102
Value_counts is especially useful for categorical data.

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:22.322
It tells us how often each category appears.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:26.012
Nunique tells us how many distinct values exist.

00:00:26.012 --> 00:00:27.592
Click Run and inspect the output.

00:00:27.592 --> 00:00:33.317
These simple functions can reveal problems very quickly.

00:00:33.317 --> 00:00:39.252
For example, suppose a channel column is expected to contain web, email, and store.

00:00:39.252 --> 00:00:42.867
If value_counts returns Web, web, WEB, and web with spaces as separate categories,

00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:48.202
we probably have a text-cleaning issue.

00:00:48.202 --> 00:00:49.882
For numeric data, describe can reveal suspicious ranges.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:55.697
If an age column has a minimum of negative five or a maximum of nine hundred,

00:00:55.697 --> 00:01:02.737
we need to investigate. EDA does not begin with complicated charts.

00:01:02.737 --> 00:01:08.942
Often it begins with simple counts, ranges, and questions about whether the values make sense in the

00:01:08.942 --> 00:01:09.747
real-world context.
